      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Champions Cup",
          "heading": "Leo Cullen's Leinster enter Champions Cup with weaker squad after summer exits",
          "body": "Leinster arguably enter the Champions Cup this weekend with a weaker squad than usual, BBC Sport NI says, after James Lowe, Rieko Ioane, Rabah Slimani and Ciaran Frawley all left over the summer. Only Frawley has been replaced in kind, by Joey Carbery, but the 30-year-old is yet to feature in his second stint because of injury. Munster, dropped into the Challenge Cup after a home defeat to Castres last season, are also starting out."
        },
        {
