          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "Kieran Hardy faces knee surgery and months out, a blow to Wales",
          "body": "Kieran Hardy, Ospreys and Wales scrum-half, needs knee surgery and faces months rather than weeks out, Ospreys transition coach Richard Kelly confirmed. Hardy, 30, was helped off in the first half of the 38-31 win at Dragons and had been expected to feature in Wales' November Tests. He was understudy to Gloucester scrum-half Tomos Williams in the 2026 Six Nations, and BBC Sport judges him a serious doubt for next year's championship too, which could intensify calls for former Wales scrum-half Gareth Davies to reverse his retirement."
        },
